,"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, obsolete","register":"not-comparable, obsolete","wordFamily":["distractable","distractee","distracter","distractful","distractive","distractor","distraught"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distract#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:608e087f513a9371ab","definition":"Insane, mad.","example":"Ol[ivia]. […] Fetch Maluolio hither, / And yet alas, novv I remember me, / They ſay poore Gentleman, he's much diſtract. […] Did he vvrite this? / Clo[wn]. I [aye] Madame. / Du[ke Orsino]. This ſauours not much of diſtraction.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, obsolete","register":"not-comparable, obsolete","wordFamily":["distractable","distractee","distracter","distractful","distractive","distractor","distraught"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distract#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/dɪˈstɹækt/"},"wordFamily":["distractable","distractee","distracter","distractful","distractive","distractor","distraught"]}